# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code sa pahinang ito ay binuo gamit ang mga sumusunod na requirement.\n"
"Inirerekomenda naming gamitin ang mga bersyong ito o mas bago.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A managed workflow job works like a batch job that you submit to an HPC scheduler. `run()` submits the job and returns a `Job` object immediately. Use the `Job` object for the tasks that `squeue`, the job's output file, and `scancel` cover on a cluster. The job keeps running after you close your notebook.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ang isang managed workflow job ay gumagana tulad ng batch job na isinusumite mo sa isang HPC scheduler. Isinusumite ng `run()` ang job at agad na nagbabalik ng `Job` object. Gamitin ang `Job` object para sa mga gawaing sakop ng `squeue`, output file ng job, at `scancel` sa isang cluster. Patuloy na tumatakbo ang job kahit isara mo ang notebook mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The examples on this page use a small workflow that reads one angle, `theta`, and fails if the angle is out of range. Upload it as described in [Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Ang mga halimbawa sa pahinang ito ay gumagamit ng maliit na workflow na nagbabasa ng isang anggulo, `theta`, at pumapalya kapag wala sa saklaw ang anggulo. I-upload ito ayon sa paliwanag sa [Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

