msgstr "Para patakbuhin ang job sa ibang compute size, ipasa ang `function_size`. Tingnan ang [Choose a size for each run](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#choose-a-size-for-each-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow a job {#follow-a-job}"
msgstr "Subaybayan ang job {#follow-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang status {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Agad pagkatapos mong tawagin ang `run()`, kadalasang `QUEUED` ang status:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Kahulugan |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | Naghihintay ang job ng compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | Nagsisimula ang workflow ng environment gamit ang compute profile ng job. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | Tumatakbo ang entrypoint ng workflow. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | Nag-ulat ang entrypoint ng stage gamit ang [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), tulad ng `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Kinansela mo ang job, at itinitigil ito ng workflow. |\n"
"| `DONE` | Matagumpay na nag-exit ang entrypoint. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | Nag-raise ng error ang entrypoint o nag-exit na may nonzero code. Tingnan ang [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Kinansela mo ang job, o umabot ito sa [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "Final na ang `DONE`, `ERROR`, at `CANCELED`, at nagbabalik ang `job.in_terminal_state()` ng `True` para sa mga ito. Ang status loop na naghihintay ng ibang value, tulad ng `SUCCEEDED`, ay hindi kailanman matatapos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Hintayin ang pagtatapos ng job {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Para hintayin hanggang matapos ang job, tawagin ang `wait_for_final_state()`. Ibinabalik nito ang final status, at kapag `verbose=True` ay ipi-print nito ang bawat pagbabago ng status. Kung magtatakda ka ng `timeout` sa segundo, mag-raise ang `wait_for_final_state()` ng `TimeoutError` kapag naubos ang oras bago matapos ang job. Patuloy na tumatakbo ang job:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng `wait_for_final_state()` ang status pagkalipas ng 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, at 32 segundo, at pagkatapos ay bawat 60 segundo, kaya nakikita nito ang pagtatapos ng maikling job sa loob ng ilang segundo at kakaunti ang request para sa mahabang job. Para mag-check sa takdang interval, ipasa ang `poll_interval` sa segundo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Basahin ang logs {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Anumang isulat ng workflow sa standard output o standard error ay napupunta sa logs ng job. Mababasa mo ang mga ito gamit ang `job.logs()` habang tumatakbo ang job, bago pa ito magkaroon ng resulta:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "Nag-a-upload ang workflow ng mga bagong log line mga bawat 15 segundo, at huling beses kapag natapos o nakansela ang job. Agad pagkatapos magsimula ng job, nagbabalik ang `job.logs()` ng `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "Itinatago ng workflow ang pinakabagong 50 MB ng logs para sa bawat job, at nagdaragdag ng linya sa itaas na nagsasabing na-truncate ang logs.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Para magpasya kung ano ang ila-log ng workflow mo, tingnan ang [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Para ipakita lang ang mga linyang tumutugma sa isang regular expression, ipasa ang `include` sa `job.filtered_logs()`. Para itago ang mga linya, ipasa ang `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Kunin ang resulta {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Naghihintay ang `job.result()` hanggang matapos ang job, saka ibinabalik ang value na ipinasa ng workflow sa [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, sinusuri ng `job.result()` ang status bawat 30 segundo at naghihintay nang walang time limit. Ipasa ang `maxwait` para limitahan ang bilang ng mga check. Halimbawa, naghihintay ang `job.result(maxwait=40)` ng mga 20 minuto. Para mag-check nang isang beses nang hindi naghihintay, ipasa ang `wait=False`. Kung huminto sa paghihintay ang `job.result()` bago matapos ang job, nagbabalik ito ng `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Tingnan kung gaano katagal ang bawat stage {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Inililista ng `job.events()` ang bawat pagbabago ng status at stage ng job kasama ang oras nito, para makita mo kung gaano katagal naghintay ang job para sa compute at gaano katagal ang bawat stage:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng mga event ang mga nakaimbak na pangalan ng status. Ang `PENDING` ay `INITIALIZING`, at ang `SUCCEEDED` ay `DONE`. Para sa QPU usage ng isang run, tingnan ang [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Hanapin ang sanhi ng error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-raise ng exception ang workflow, nagtatapos ang job na may `ERROR` status. Halimbawa, patakbuhin ang workflow gamit ang anggulong tinatanggihan nito:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng logs ang traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Kung [nag-uulat ng mga error ang workflow gamit ang `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), basahin ang mga ito gamit ang `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, at basahin ang mga mensahe nila gamit ang `job.error_message()`. Para sa job na walang naiulat na error, nagbabalik ang `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` ng walang laman na listahan, at nagbabalik ang `job.error_message()` ng `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Pamahalaan ang mga job {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Mag-cancel ng job {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-cancel ng job gamit ang `job.cancel()`. Magiging `CANCELING` ang status habang itinitigil ng workflow ang job, at pagkatapos ay `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabalik ang `job.cancel()` ng mensahe tungkol sa job at sa mga [naka-link na QPU job](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs) nito, na sinusubukan din nitong i-cancel. Para sa tumatakbong job, nagpapadala ang workflow ng `SIGTERM` sa entrypoint mo. Para mag-save ng partial results, tingnan ang [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Kung tapos na ang job, nagbabalik ang `job.cancel()` ng `Job already in terminal state.` at walang binabago.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Maghanap ng job mula sa bagong session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `Job` object at ang workflow ay umiiral lang sa kasalukuyan mong Python session. Pagkatapos mong i-restart ang notebook kernel, ipasa ang naka-save na job ID sa `client.job()`, o ilista ang mga kamakailan mong job gamit ang `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `client.jobs()` ang 10 pinakabagong job mo, pinakabago muna. I-filter ito gamit ang `function`, `status` (mula sa [status table](#check-the-status)), o `created_after` (isang ISO 8601 timestamp), at mag-page through gamit ang `limit` at `offset`. Para ilista ang mga workflow na na-upload mo, tawagin ang `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "Inililista rin ng [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table sa IBM Quantum Platform ang mga job mo, kasama ang status, compute profile, at run time ng mga ito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Time limit {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Kinakansela ng managed workflow ang job na tumatakbo nang mahigit 24 oras, at nagtatapos ang job na may `CANCELED` status. Sa mahahabang run, [mag-save ng mga checkpoint sa file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) para hindi mawala ang trabaho mo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "I-troubleshoot ang mga job {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Sanhi |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `run()` na may `Code: 429` at `Active job limit reached.` | Naabot mo ang [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Hintayin munang matapos ang ilang job, o [i-cancel](#cancel-a-job) ang mga job na hindi mo na kailangan. |\n"
"| Nananatiling `QUEUED` ang job, at nagbabala ang `run()` na `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | Hindi magsisimula ang job hangga't hindi inaalis ang block sa account, plan, o subscription mo. Makipag-ugnayan sa administrator mo. |\n"
"| Nagbabalik ang `job.logs()` ng `No logs yet.` | Naka-queue ang job o kakasimula lang. Maghintay ng mga 15 segundo. |\n"
"| Nagbabalik ang `job.result()` ng `{}` | Hindi pa tapos ang job, nakansela ito, o walang na-save na resulta. Tingnan ang [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| Nagbabalik ang `job.error_message()` ng `{}` | Nag-raise ng exception ang workflow nang hindi nag-uulat ng error. Basahin ang traceback gamit ang `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| `CANCELED` ang job, pero hindi mo ito kinansela | Umabot ang job sa [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"

